Chapter: ActSpan

 An act block used to take `synthetic-span` -- 0,0 -- because the CST
 `ActExpr` carries no token of its own. That put the one position-less
 node exactly where the most common effect error lands: `check-def`
 reports CDX2031 against `aexpr-span (def.body)`, and for any def whose
 body is an act block the diagnostic printed with no line:column at all.
 Most effectful code in the language has an act block for a body.

 The block now takes its first statement's span. On this chapter the
 CDX2031 reports at 48:5 -- the `print-line-uni` inside `needs-console`
 below -- where it used to report nowhere.

 That 48 is a line in THIS FILE, which is a second fix and not a given.
 The compiler numbers diagnostics against the assembled unit -- every
 cited chapter, then the source -- so a position was off by however many
 lines the dependencies ran to, and a file citing one foreword chapter
 reported its line 11 as 214. A cite-less file was right only by
 accident. Both assemblers map back now (`Convert-DiagLine`,
 `quire-map.ps1`), which matters here because the battery builds its own
 unit and writes its own log; had only `compile.ps1` mapped, this pin
 would pass by hand and fail in the battery.

 The sidecar is `CDX2031@48:5`, not a bare `CDX2031`, and the difference
 is the whole point of this file. A bare code checks only that the error
 fired, and CDX2031 fired before the fix too -- it just fired with no
 line:column, because a 0,0 span prints no prefix at all. A code-only
 check therefore passes against the exact compiler this test exists to
 catch. The `@line:col` form is what can fail on a lost position, and
 `build/test.ps1` grew it for this.

 Run rather than assumed: against this compile's log, `CDX2031@48:5`
 matches, `CDX2031@10:5` does not, and bare `CDX2031` matches either way.
 The pin discriminates; the bare code does not.

 The position moves if the prose above it does. That is the cost of
 pinning a line number and it is worth paying here -- a wrong number
 fails loudly and is a one-character fix, where a lost position failed
 silently for as long as this defect existed.

Section: Entry

  helper : Integer -> Integer
  helper (n) = n + 1

  needs-console : Integer -> Integer
  needs-console (n) = act
    print-line-uni "declares no Console but performs it"
    helper n
  end

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
    print-line-uni (show (needs-console 1))
  end
